<title>USA: Pa. Gov. declares 8 counties disaster after snow.</title>
<headline>Pa. Gov. declares 8 counties disaster after snow.</headline>
<dateline>HARRISBURG 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pennsylvania Gov. Tom Ridge declared a disaster in eight northeastern counties after a storm dumped up to 30 inches of snow.</p>
<p>The declaration covers Carbon, Chester, Lackawanna, Luzerne, Monroe, Pike, Schuylkill, and Wayne Counties.</p>
<p>The move cuts red tape and speeds the process for seeking disaster aid from the federal government if necessary.</p>
